{
  "engine": "payroll/employee-pipeline",
  "rateSet": "structural-fiction-v1",
  "_readme": [
    "Structural vectors (ADR-0018 §3) for payroll.md §4.5's eight-stage pipeline, computed",
    "against the fictional rate set — including the BPJS and tax sections, because stages 4",
    "and 6 invoke those calculators in place. Nothing here is or resembles Indonesian",
    "regulation (overtime divisor 100, basis floor one half, line unit 100).",
    "What these pin: the statutory bases as category formulas (BR-PAY-003), the 75%-floor",
    "shape on the overtime basis (BR-PAY-004, at the fictional half), proration touching",
    "lines but never the bases (BR-PAY-013, BR-PAY-027), employer premiums reaching taxable",
    "assembly while deduction lines never do (BR-PAY-026), the THR entitlement ladder",
    "(BR-PAY-015), the gross-up line pair footing, the final-settlement composition, and",
    "net = Σ earning − Σ deduction over rounded lines with employer_cost outside both",
    "(BR-PAY-012).",
    "A failing vector is a code defect until a human re-verifies it and records why it",
    "changed; a vector is never edited to make a test pass (testing-strategy §6.1).",
    "Input mirrors PayrollEmployeeInput minus `parameters` (injected by the runner from the",
    "declared rateSet). Expected omits `trace`; the runner asserts the net foots from the",
    "lines themselves on every vector."
  ],
